From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:25:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] cabextract: fetch the sources from GitHub

www.cabextract.org.uk, the only site serving cabextract-1.11.tar.gz (no
Buildroot mirror copy), timed out from a CI runner and the build stopped
at host-cabextract. The same sources are the cabextract/ directory of
kyz/libmspack on GitHub, tag v1.11: use that archive with a subdirectory
and autoreconf (the git tree has no configure script; AM_ICONV needs
gettext's m4 files). The host tool builds with the bundled libmspack
sources, since there is no host-libmspack package.

001-fixfnmatch.patch edited config.h.in, which autoreconf now generates:
the configure cache variable ac_cv_func_fnmatch_works=yes has the same
effect for the cross-compiled target (AC_REPLACE_FNMATCH cannot run its
test there and would substitute its own fnmatch).

Verified: autoreconf, configure and make from that tree give cabextract
1.11, with the bundled sources and with an external libmspack.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019W6m4A3E7pevQ1bs91jPmM
---
 .../utils/cabextract/001-fixfnmatch.patch     | 13 ----------
 .../batocera/utils/cabextract/cabextract.mk   | 26 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 package/batocera/utils/cabextract/001-fixfnmatch.patch

diff --git a/package/batocera/utils/cabextract/001-fixfnmatch.patch b/package/batocera/utils/cabextract/001-fixfnmatch.patch
deleted file mode 100644
index e54eafc1..00000000
--- a/package/batocera/utils/cabextract/001-fixfnmatch.patch
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,13 +0,0 @@
-diff --git a/config.h.in b/config.h.in
-index c2967ec..702df9f 100644
---- a/config.h.in
-+++ b/config.h.in
-@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@
- #undef const
- 
- /* Define to rpl_fnmatch if the replacement function should be used. */
--#undef fnmatch
-+//#undef fnmatch
- 
- /* Define to `__inline__' or `__inline' if that's what the C compiler
-    calls it, or to nothing if 'inline' is not supported under any name.  */
diff --git a/package/batocera/utils/cabextract/cabextract.mk b/package/batocera/utils/cabextract/cabextract.mk
index 05d69182..1b8bff65 100644
--- a/package/batocera/utils/cabextract/cabextract.mk
+++ b/package/batocera/utils/cabextract/cabextract.mk
@@ -4,12 +4,30 @@
 #
 ################################################################################
 
+# The release tarballs live on www.cabextract.org.uk only (no Buildroot
+# mirror), and that site is not always reachable. The same 1.11 sources are
+# the cabextract/ directory of the libmspack repository on GitHub, tagged
+# v1.11; its mspack/ symlinks point into ../libmspack, hence the whole
+# repository and a subdirectory. The git tree has no configure script.
 CABEXTRACT_VERSION = 1.11
-CABEXTRACT_SOURCE = cabextract-$(CABEXTRACT_VERSION).tar.gz
-CABEXTRACT_SITE = https://www.cabextract.org.uk
-CABEXTRACT_DEPENDENCIES = libmspack
-
+CABEXTRACT_SOURCE = libmspack-v$(CABEXTRACT_VERSION).tar.gz
+CABEXTRACT_SITE = $(call github,kyz,libmspack,v$(CABEXTRACT_VERSION))
+CABEXTRACT_SUBDIR = cabextract
+CABEXTRACT_AUTORECONF = YES
+# AM_ICONV in configure.ac comes from gettext's m4 files
+CABEXTRACT_DEPENDENCIES = libmspack host-gettext
 CABEXTRACT_CONF_OPTS = --with-external-libmspack
+# AC_REPLACE_FNMATCH cannot run its test when cross compiling and would
+# define fnmatch to its own rpl_fnmatch (what 001-fixfnmatch.patch undid in
+# config.h.in, a file that autoreconf now generates): the target's fnmatch
+# works.
+CABEXTRACT_CONF_ENV = ac_cv_func_fnmatch_works=yes
+
+# There is no host-libmspack: the host tool (it unpacks the Xbox pad
+# firmware .cab files at build time) uses the libmspack sources bundled
+# in the same archive.
+HOST_CABEXTRACT_DEPENDENCIES = host-gettext
+HOST_CABEXTRACT_CONF_OPTS = --without-external-libmspack
 
 $(eval $(autotools-package))
 $(eval $(host-autotools-package))
